(version 1)

# castle-carrier v5 custom design rules - generated by gen/make_pcb.py
# from gen/design.py.  DO NOT EDIT.
#
# Fabricator:  JLCPCB JLC04161H-7628, 4-layer FR-4,
#              1 oz outer / 0.5 oz inner copper
# Capability:  https://jlcpcb.com/capabilities/pcb-capabilities
# Fetched:     2026-09-03 (rules) / 2026-09-04 (stackup)
#              2026-09-05 (re-read against the MULTILAYER column, which is
#              the one a four-layer board is built to - gen/design.py
#              DESIGN_RULES has both columns side by side)
#
# KiCad keeps the NUMERIC limits (track width, clearance, annular ring,
# hole-to-hole, edge clearance, silk height and stroke) in the project file,
# castle-carrier.kicad_pro, not here.  gen/design.py DESIGN_RULES is where
# they are written from, and README.md "Design rules" prints the vendor's
# figure beside the project's for every one of them.
#
# This file holds only rules KiCad cannot express as a number.  v3 had five:
# one per solderable Wuerth standoff, relaxing hole_clearance to 0 mm because
# that part's 6.0 mm solder ring touches its own 3.7 mm locating-boss hole by
# the manufacturer's own drawing.  The posts went with the Feather, and v3.1
# to v5 stage 3 needed none at all.
#
# V5 STAGE 3b ADDS ONE, AND IT IS A PER-NET RULE RATHER THAN AN EXEMPTION.
# The USB pair's fan-out at J16 necks to
# 0.20 mm, and that is DESIGN INTENT rather than a router accident:
# a USB-C receptacle presents D- and D+ interleaved on a 0.50 mm pitch, so
# one half of the pair has to change half-plane under the shell, and
# 0.35 mm of copper centred on a 0.30 mm signal pad leaves 0.175 mm to
# the pad beside it against a 0.20 mm clearance rule.  0.20 mm leaves
# 0.25 mm.  The BOARD-WIDE minimum connection width stays at 0.25 mm
# and is unchanged; the rule below lowers it for USB_DP and USB_DM and for
# nothing else, so a narrow neck anywhere on any other net is still a DRC
# error.  gen/audit_v5.py check 45 is the other half of this and is STRICTER,
# not looser: it bounds how much of the pair may be necked (9.0 mm a
# half), how far from J16 it may happen (6.0 mm) and fails any
# segment that is neither the run width nor the neck width.

(rule "USB pair fan-out neck at J16"
	(constraint connection_width (min 0.20mm))
	(condition "A.NetName == 'USB_DP' || A.NetName == 'USB_DM'"))
